on, monitoring, reforms, violence prevention, and credible elections; P5 provides registration-to-results sequence and tribunal. | S6 P6 SCS second term, week 1; S5 P5 SCS second term, weeks 4 and 7 | Direct coverage | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | Petition process is combined from adjacent-grade material. Strictly nonpartisan; neutrality review required. |\n| p6-socs-06 | The Nigerian Judiciary — Protecting Rights | S11 Supreme Court of Nigeria official site; S7 Lagos State MoE legacy P5 Civic; S1 context | P6 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): judiciary, rule of law, and rights protection | Legacy curriculum covers the arms of government and separation of powers; the official Supreme Court source establishes its apex/appellate role and constitutional rights jurisdiction. | S7 p. 29; S11 Jurisdiction/About; S1 p. 3 ethical/social responsibility | Enrichment | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | No direct P6 public SCS judiciary objective was found. Court structure, including state/federal, Sharia, customary, magistrate, High Court, Court of Appeal, and Supreme Court distinctions, requires legal fact-checking and careful non-ladder framing. |\n| p6-socs-07 | Social Cohesion — Inter-ethnic and Inter-religious Tolerance | S7 Lagos State MoE legacy P6 Social Studies; S4 public unified SCS P4; S1 context | P6 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): tolerance, peace, diversity, and cohesion | Public sources cover religious intolerance, inter-ethnic relations, tolerance, cooperation, dialogue, respect for beliefs, and peaceful coexistence. | S7 pp. 256–258 and 263–265; S4 P4 SCS first term, Beliefs and Tradition; S1 p. 3 | Direct coverage | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | Historical-coexistence claims and mediation bodies need sources during authoring. Do not identify live conflicts, sects, or armed groups. |\n| p6-socs-08 | Migration — Internal and International | S5 public unified SCS P5; S6 public unified SCS P6; S7 legacy P5/P6 Social Studies | P6 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): migration, displacement, employment, and protection | Public schemes distinguish migration from trafficking and connect displacement to conflict/economic factors; legacy material covers employment-driven movement and settlement pressures. | S5 P5 SCS third term, Introduction to Human Trafficking; S6 P6 SCS second term, weeks 8–10; S7 pp. 249–251 and 259 | Enrichment | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | No direct P6 migration/IDP/refugee objective was found. UNHCR and displaced-person rights are enrichment and require authoritative sourcing during authoring. |\n| p6-socs-09 | Safety and Security — Staying Safe as a Citizen | S4 public unified SCS P4; S5 public unified SCS P5; S6 public unified SCS P6 | P6 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): personal safety, neighbourhood security, and safe choices | Public schemes cover neighbourhood safety, reporting, adult help, cyber awareness, risk assessment, safe choices, and resilience. | S4 P4 SCS third term, Neighbourhood Security/Accident Response; S5 P5 SCS third term, Neighbourhood Security; S6 P6 SCS third term, Safe and Healthy Choices | Enrichment | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | Brief intentionally narrows the content to immediate personal safety and prohibits profiling, named groups, tactics, recruitment signs, and conflict-zone examples. Full Hausa sign-off required. |\n| p6-socs-10 | Technology and Society | S1 NERDC implementation context; S6 public unified P6 SCS and Basic Digital Literacy | P6 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): digital citizenship, communication, and online safety | S1 requires digital competencies and responsible technology use; public P6 material covers digital financial services, online safety, internet/social-media safety, privacy, and cyber risks. | S1 pp. 1–3; S6 P6 SCS second term, week 3 and third term, week 8; S6 P6 Basic Digital Literacy, Internet/Social Media Safety | Combined coverage | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | Partly cross-curricular. Cyberbullying is not explicit in the cited SCS section but fits the public digital-safety sequence. |\n| p6-socs-11 | Civic Role Models in Nigeria | S7 Lagos State MoE legacy P6 Civic; S6 public unified SCS P6 | P6 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): national service, role models, and civic leadership | Public P6 civic material covers national honours, selfless service, award recipients, patriotism, and nationalists’ achievements; public SCS asks pupils to become role models and agents of change. | S7 pp. 32–33; S6 P6 SCS third term, weeks 9–10 | Combined coverage | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | The five named Nigerians are Architect-selected, not a public scheme list. Keep biography to one sentence and focus on civic contribution; neutrality review required. |\n| p6-socs-12 | Population Growth and Civic Responsibility | S7 Lagos State MoE legacy P5/P6 Social Studies; S6 public unified P6 demography | P6 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): population, services, resources, and planning | Public sources cover population growth, water/housing demand, resource use, census, density, planning, and resource allocation. | S7 pp. 250–252 and 261; S6 P6 Mathematics second term, Demography & Money I | Combined coverage | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | Partly cross-curricular. Any population statistic must carry a reference year and authoritative source; avoid coercive family-size messaging. |\n| p6-socs-13 | Entrepreneurship and Self-Reliance | S6 public unified SCS P6; S7 Lagos State MoE legacy P4/P6 Social Studies; S1 context | P6 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): entrepreneurship, work, and national development | Public P6 SCS covers entrepreneurship, financial goals, youth innovation, nation building, and personal commitment; legacy source covers self-employment skills and loans. | S6 P6 SCS second term, week 2 and third term, week 9; S7 pp. 233 and 259; S1 p. 3 | Direct coverage | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | Bank of Agriculture and BOI are brief-selected institutions and require current official verification at authoring time. |\n| p6-socs-14 | Peace Education and Conflict Prevention | S7 Lagos State MoE legacy P6 Social Studies; S1 context | P6 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): peace, tolerance, cooperation, and conflict resolution | Public P6 state scheme defines peace education and covers tolerance, cooperation, shared responsibility, communal effort, and national unity. | S7 pp. 263–265, Group Conflict and Peace Education; S1 p. 3 | Direct coverage | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | UNICEF-framework reference is enrichment. Avoid operational conflict details and current conflict actors. |\n| p6-socs-15 | Revision and Consolidation — Bridge to JSS1 | S6 public unified SCS P6 | P6 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): consolidation and secondary-school citizenship | Public P6 SCS closes with preparation for secondary-school citizenship, comprehensive review, role modelling, leadership, and life-long learning. | S6 P6 SCS third term, weeks 10–12 | Direct coverage | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | The P3–P6 recap is AJAMIX-specific consolidation. |\n\n## Matrix totals and validation summary\n\n- Total rows: **60**.\n- Grade distribution: **P3 15; P4 15; P5 15; P6 15**.\n- Duplicate module IDs: **0**.\n- Missing brief IDs/titles: **0**.\n- Missing classifications: **0**.\n- Classification distribution: **Direct coverage 19; Combined coverage 21; Enrichment 20**.\n- Missing verification statuses: **0**.\n- `mapping uncertain — no public source found`: **0 rows**.\n- Important limitation: zero “mapping uncertain” flags means each proposed module has at least some cited public support; it does **not** mean any row is verified against the official NERDC grade document.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
