{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/ARCHITECT-BRIEF-SOCS-P3-P6.md | sed -n '251,350p'\"","aggregated_output":"   251\t  \"targetAudience\": \"youth\",\n   252\t  \"gapTeaser\": null,\n   253\t  \"chainNext\": null,\n   254\t  \"isChainLeaf\": true,\n   255\t  \"useTodayPrompt\": null\n   256\t}\n   257\t```\n   258\t\n   259\t**Field rules**\n   260\t- `gradeband`: `\"p3\"` / `\"p4\"` / `\"p5\"` / `\"p6\"` — lowercase.\n   261\t- `subject`: `\"Social Studies\"` (unchanged from P1/P2 to preserve app.js rendering).\n   262\t- `subjectHa`: `\"Nazarin Zamantakewa\"` — exactly this casing, this term, every module.\n   263\t- `id`: `p<band>-socs-NN`, zero-padded, sequential within each band. `moduleNumber` 1..15 per band.\n   264\t- All Ajami fields = `null`. `ajami_validated` = `false`.\n   265\t- `audioFile` / `imageCard`: placeholder paths; path must match module id.\n   266\t- `track`: `\"formal\"`, `targetAudience`: `\"youth\"`.\n   267\t- **Flat leaves:** `chainNext: null`, `isChainLeaf: true`, `gapTeaser: null`, `useTodayPrompt: null`.\n   268\t- **Exactly 2** `microPauses`; **exactly 5** `quizQuestions`.\n   269\t\n   270\t**Quiz contract — Social and Citizenship Studies is static Q&A, not parameterized formulas**\n   271\t- `variableRanges`: `{a:{min:0,max:0}, b:{min:0,max:0}}` (unused placeholder — match P1/P2 pattern exactly).\n   272\t- `answerFormula`: the **literal correct Hausa answer string**.\n   273\t- `distractorFormulas`: **three plausible wrong Hausa answer strings**.\n   274\t- **The correct answer must not appear among the three distractors.**\n   275\t- `microPauses[].options[]` includes the `correctAnswer`; the `correctAnswer` appears **exactly once** in `options`.\n   276\t- Cross-module consistency: any Hausa word/phrase reused as `correctAnswer`, `options`, or `distractorFormulas` must use one single, correct hooked spelling across every module and every field. Inconsistent spelling silently breaks scoring.\n   277\t\n   278\t---\n   279\t\n   280\t## 9. Hausa terminology gates\n   281\t\n   282\t### Locked terms (all prior arcs — apply here)\n   283\t\n   284\t- `kaɗan` — \"little/a bit\" (never `kadan`).\n   285\t- `riƙa` — habitual marker.\n   286\t- `ɓoye` — \"to hide.\"\n   287\t- `ɓera` — \"rat/mouse.\"\n   288\t- `ƙwai` — \"egg.\"\n   289\t- `tambarin Nijeriya` — coat of arms (ruled P2-socs-11).\n   290\t- `Nazarin Zamantakewa` — subject label.\n   291\t\n   292\t### Social and Citizenship Studies terms locked 2026-07-16 (M1 pilot review)\n   293\t\n   294\t- `ƙaramar hukuma` — Local Government Area / LGA. This is the main learner-facing term; `LGA` may appear once as a parenthetical acronym on first mention in a module, never as the primary term thereafter.\n   295\t- `ɗan ƙasa` (singular) / `ƴan ƙasa` (plural) — citizen / citizens.\n   296\t- `muhalli` — environment.\n   297\t- `ƙananan yankuna` — ward / sub-area, P3-appropriate descriptive phrase. Do not introduce a more technical \"ward\" term until election/governance modules (P4+) require it — raise that as a fresh open question when reached.\n   298\t- `kansila` — councillor, when naming the office directly; `wakilin yanki` — councillor, descriptive/informal register. Both correct, context-dependent.\n   299\t- `hidimar jama'a` — a public service (singular instance); `ayyukan jama'a` — public works/services (plural, general sense). Keep the distinction; do not use interchangeably.\n   300\t- `rigar kariya ta ruwa` — life jacket. The plain `rigar kariya` (\"protective garment\") is too generic and must not be used for this meaning.\n   301\t- `mai shela` — town crier.\n   302\t- `ganga ko kalangu` — drum, broad/general reference; `kalangu` alone — specifically the talking drum. Use the narrower term only when the talking drum specifically is meant.\n   303\t- `sufuri` — transportation; `sadarwa` — communication. Locked as section-heading terms for the whole P3–P6 arc.\n   304\t\n   305\t### Social and Citizenship Studies terms locked 2026-07-16 (M2 P3-complete review)\n   306\t\n   307\t- `rediyo`, `talabijin`, `waya`, `wayar hannu`, `intanet` — approved as the locked modern-communication device terms.\n   308\t- `gurɓata` — approved descriptive wording for pollution/contamination at P3 level. A formal \"pollution\" noun remains open and deferred until P5 (`p5-socs-03`) if needed there.\n   309\t- `kiwo` — approved as the P3 learner-facing livestock/rearing category term.\n   310\t- `musayar kaya da kaya` — approved descriptive phrase for barter at P3 level; not replaced with a technical/borrowed noun.\n   311\t- Cultural heritage stays descriptive for now (e.g. `al'adunmu`, explained through food/dress/language) — `gadon al'adu` is NOT locked or forced; do not introduce it unless separately ruled.\n   312\t- UNCRC — do not introduce the acronym or a formal Hausa title for the convention unless a later module specifically requires it.\n   313\t- `Eid al-Fitr`, `Eid al-Adha`, `Christmas`, `New Yam` — approved to remain as proper names (not translated or replaced with generic Hausa terms).\n   314\t\n   315\t### Terms requiring user ruling in later dispatches\n   316\t\n   317\tThese must be raised as open questions in milestone reports, resolved by the user, and locked before the next dispatch. Codex does not interpolate a term — it flags and waits.\n   318\t\n   319\t| Concept | Candidate / note |\n   320\t|---------|-----------------|\n   321\t| Democracy / democratic | `dimokuradiyya` common in Hausa media — confirm |\n   322\t| Constitution | `kundin tsarin mulki` — confirm hooks and usage |\n   323\t| Election / voting | `zaɓe` well-attested; `jefa ƙuri'a` for \"casting a vote\" — confirm |\n   324\t| Pollution | Hausa term or borrowed — user to rule |\n   325\t| Migration | Hausa descriptive phrase or borrowed — user to rule |\n   326\t| Globalisation | Hausa descriptive phrase or borrowed — user to rule |\n   327\t| Drug / substance abuse | `magani` = medicine generically; term for misused substance — user to rule |\n   328\t| Sustainability | Hausa descriptive phrase — user to rule |\n   329\t| Conflict resolution | phrase to lock — user to rule |\n   330\t| Ward (technical/electoral sense) | raise when P4+ governance modules require a more precise term than `ƙananan yankuna` |\n   331\t\n   332\tThis list is not exhaustive. Codex raises every uncertain term immediately; it does not interpolate.\n   333\t\n   334\t---\n   335\t\n   336\t## 10. Build sequence and milestones\n   337\t\n   338\t| Milestone | Scope | Pre-condition |\n   339\t|-----------|-------|---------------|\n   340\t| **M0 — Preflight** | Alignment matrix for all 60 modules; M0 script; live count read | Architect approves alignment matrix before M1 dispatch |\n   341\t| **M1 — P3 pilot** | `p3-socs-01..06`, source-only candidate | Architect approval of M1 report |\n   342\t| **M2 — P3 complete** | `p3-socs-07..15`, source-only candidate | Architect approval of M2 report; terminology from M1 locked |\n   343\t| **M3 — P4 complete** | `p4-socs-01..15`, source-only candidate | Architect approval of M3 report |\n   344\t| **M4 — P5 complete** | `p5-socs-01..15`, source-only candidate; `p5-socs-07` sign-off | Architect approval + user sign-off on `p5-socs-07` |\n   345\t| **M5 — P6 complete** | `p6-socs-01..15`, source-only candidate; `p6-socs-03` + `p6-socs-09` sign-off | Architect approval + user sign-off on both sensitive modules |\n   346\t| **Integration** | Guarded merge of each approved band into `content.json` | Only after user Hausa validation of that band's source candidate |\n   347\t\n   348\tM1 dispatch is **source-only**: Codex creates `tools/p3-batch/p3-socs-pilot.json` (6 modules); does not touch `app/content.json`. Architect validates using a **temporary merged copy**, not the live file.\n   349\t\n   350\t---\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
