{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/ARCHITECT-BRIEF-SOCS-P3-P6.md | sed -n '351,491p'\"","aggregated_output":"   351\t\n   352\t## 11. Integration sequence (per milestone)\n   353\t\n   354\t1. Codex creates a **source-only candidate** batch file (e.g. `tools/p3-batch/p3-socs.json`). Does not touch `app/content.json`.\n   355\t2. Architect runs all gates against the candidate on a **temporary merged copy** (`node -e \"const d=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('app/content.json')); d.modules.push(...batch); fs.writeFileSync('/tmp/content-candidate.json', JSON.stringify(d,null,2))\"` → validate against temp file). `app/content.json` remains unchanged.\n   356\t3. Architect approves milestone; user reviews Hausa terminology and all sensitive-topic modules.\n   357\t4. Codex patches corrections on approved user feedback.\n   358\t5. Architect revalidates the patched candidate.\n   359\t6. Only then: a **guarded, idempotent Node script** appends the approved batch into live `app/content.json` (dedup by `id`, preserve formatting, run validator immediately after). No hand-editing of `content.json`.\n   360\t7. Architect confirms: validator exit 0, correct total count, byte-equivalence of all pre-existing modules.\n   361\t\n   362\t**Unvalidated Hausa is never written into the production `app/content.json`.**\n   363\t\n   364\t---\n   365\t\n   366\t## 12. Definition of Done (per milestone)\n   367\t\n   368\tA milestone candidate is **build-complete** (ready for human validation — NOT shippable) when all of the following hold:\n   369\t\n   370\t**Structure gates**\n   371\t1. Every module matches the §8 schema contract, key-for-key.\n   372\t2. `node app/tools/validate-content.mjs` on the temporary merged copy exits **0**.\n   373\t3. Only `modules[]` grew in the temporary merge — no reordering, edits, or deletions to existing modules, gradeBands, glossary, or activities.\n   374\t4. **Zero changes** to any runtime file: `app/app.js`, `app/quiz-engine.js`, `app/styles.css`, `app/index.html`, `app/sw.js`, `app/bootstrap.js` (if present). Confirmed by mtime + `shasum -a 256` on each before/after (content checksums, not git — git hangs).\n   375\t5. IDs unique; `moduleNumber` sequential per subject per band; no gaps.\n   376\t\n   377\t**Content gates**\n   378\t6. **Word-count:** `textExplanationHa` is 120–170 words per module, every module. Build the word-count assertion into the per-band structure-check script from the start (lesson from the Math arc Slice 3 retro).\n   379\t7. **Audio-explanation alignment:** audio script content aligns materially with `textExplanationHa` — not a copy, but teaching the same facts.\n   380\t8. **Micro-pause text match:** `[PAUSE 1]` wording in `audioScript` must exactly match `microPauses[0].questionHa`; `[PAUSE 2]` must exactly match `microPauses[1].questionHa`. These are not summaries — they must be identical.\n   381\t9. **Micro-pause answer integrity:** `correctAnswer` appears exactly once in `options[]` for each micro-pause.\n   382\t10. **Quiz answer integrity:** `answerFormula` does not appear in `distractorFormulas[]`.\n   383\t11. **Quiz fact grounding:** every quiz question's correct answer must be taught in `textExplanationHa` or the audio script of the same module.\n   384\t12. **Unique Q5:** the fifth quiz question is topic-specific to this module — not a generic \"What is [subject]?\" filler.\n   385\t13. **Unique OUTRO:** `[OUTRO]` is topic-specific to this module — not a generic boilerplate close.\n   386\t14. **No generic revision-module filler:** revision modules (`*-socs-15`) must provide a genuine consolidation question set, not placeholder text.\n   387\t15. **Raw-English leakage:** no English words appear in `textExplanationHa`, `audioScript` (outside bracketed script markers `[INTRO]` etc.), or quiz fields, unless the word is an official borrowed term (e.g. `LGA`, `internet`) that the user has confirmed as standard in Hausa use for this concept.\n   388\t\n   389\t**Hausa gates**\n   390\t16. **Hooked-letter lint:** `node tools/p2-batch/hook-lint.mjs <batch-file.json>` exits **0** (zero ERRORS). WARNINGS listed explicitly in milestone report as open questions for the user.\n   391\t17. **Cross-module quiz-answer consistency:** for every Hausa string reused across quiz-answer-matching fields within the batch, grep for every instance and confirm identical spelling. Words checked and results reported in milestone report — not just \"lint passed.\"\n   392\t18. **Within-module redundancy check:** run the decimal-aware redundancy checker (`tools/p1-batch/check-within-module-redundancy.mjs`) against all modules in the batch. Zero findings, or findings listed for user adjudication.\n   393\t19. **Manual close-paraphrase review:** Codex reports any sentence pairs across modules in the batch that are near-duplicate paraphrases but not caught by the automated checker.\n   394\t\n   395\t**Sensitive-topic gates**\n   396\t20. **Neutrality attestation:** for every module in §5's neutrality-review list, a one-line Codex attestation in the milestone report confirming no prescriptive, hierarchical, or group-attributing framing was used.\n   397\t21. **Sensitive-topic flags:** `p5-socs-07`, `p6-socs-03`, `p6-socs-09` include an explicit open-question in their milestone report directing the user to review full Hausa draft before slice approval. Family-planning content is prohibited unless the official grade document later confirms it and the user explicitly reopens that scope.\n   398\t\n   399\t**Scope gates**\n   400\t22. **P1/P2 Social Studies frozen:** `p1-socs-01..15` and `p2-socs-01..15` byte-equivalent before and after the temporary merge. Confirmed by `shasum -a 256` on every pre-existing Social Studies module object.\n   401\t23. **All pre-existing module objects frozen:** not only P1/P2 Social Studies — all previously live modules must remain byte-equivalent.\n   402\t\n   403\tOnly after all 23 gates pass is the candidate handed to the user's Hausa validation gate (Gates 3–4 of `docs/VALIDATION-CHECKLIST.md`). The candidate is not shippable until the user clears that gate.\n   404\t\n   405\t---\n   406\t\n   407\t## 13. Milestone reporting protocol (Codex → Architect)\n   408\t\n   409\tEach dispatch must produce two output paths:\n   410\t- `--output-last-message`: brief summary (module list, exit codes, counts).\n   411\t- Detailed report file at `tasks/<date>-<milestone>-report.md`: full gate results.\n   412\t\n   413\tArchitect independently verifies all 23 gates before approving any milestone. Never rubber-stamps Codex self-report.\n   414\t\n   415\tRequired report sections:\n   416\t\n   417\t1. Module list (ID + titleEn + titleHa).\n   418\t2. Validator output (exit code, temporary-merge count before/after).\n   419\t3. Hook-lint output (exit code, ERRORS count, WARNINGS list with context).\n   420\t4. Word-count summary (min/max; any out-of-range flagged).\n   421\t5. Audio-explanation alignment attestation.\n   422\t6. Micro-pause text match confirmation (exact string comparison for both pauses).\n   423\t7. Quiz answer integrity check (Q5 uniqueness, OUTRO uniqueness, no answer-in-distractor violations).\n   424\t8. Quiz fact-grounding check.\n   425\t9. English-leakage scan result.\n   426\t10. Cross-module quiz-answer consistency check (words checked + result).\n   427\t11. Within-module redundancy check result.\n   428\t12. Close-paraphrase manual review notes.\n   429\t13. Neutrality attestation for each module in the review list.\n   430\t14. Sensitive-topic flags (if applicable).\n   431\t15. Terminology open questions (any new Hausa term uncertain; awaiting user ruling).\n   432\t16. `shasum -a 256 app/content.json` before and after (temporary merge; live file unchanged).\n   433\t17. Engine-file checksum confirmation (all six runtime files unchanged).\n   434\t18. Alignment matrix column for each module (curriculum version, strand, source page, classification) — M0 and M1 report; subsequent reports may reference M0 matrix and note any changes.\n   435\t\n   436\t---\n   437\t\n   438\t## 14. Image-manifest deliverable\n   439\t\n   440\tEach milestone must also produce an image/diagram-needs manifest to the same schema used under `tools/image-manifest/`. These are produced alongside the source candidate, before guarded integration:\n   441\t\n   442\t- `tools/image-manifest/p3-socs-image-manifest.json` (M1+M2)\n   443\t- `tools/image-manifest/p4-socs-image-manifest.json` (M3)\n   444\t- `tools/image-manifest/p5-socs-image-manifest.json` (M4)\n   445\t- `tools/image-manifest/p6-socs-image-manifest.json` (M5)\n   446\t\n   447\tFor every module, the manifest entry specifies:\n   448\t\n   449\t| Field | Content |\n   450\t|-------|---------|\n   451\t| `moduleId` | e.g. `p3-socs-01` |\n   452\t| `titleEn` | English module title |\n   453\t| `visualType` | map / diagram / illustration / portrait / comparison / symbol |\n   454\t| `depictEn` | What the image should show (English, specific) |\n   455\t| `hausaLabels` | Hausa text labels drawn verbatim from the lesson — not invented |\n   456\t| `culturalContext` | Northern Nigerian setting requirements |\n   457\t| `neutralityConstraints` | What must not be depicted (specific to this module) |\n   458\t| `prohibitedImagery` | Any imagery that would violate the §5 sensitivity rules |\n   459\t| `safetyNote` | If applicable (e.g. no real court logos, no political party imagery) |\n   460\t| `notes` | Map requirements, symbol requirements, portrait/diversity requirements |\n   461\t\n   462\tNo images are rendered in this content-build workstream. The manifests are design-intent records for the future image-generation workstream.\n   463\t\n   464\t---\n   465\t\n   466\t## 15. Integration mechanics\n   467\t\n   468\t- Author each band as a standalone batch file first; merge via idempotent Node script.\n   469\t- **Never git** — repo git hangs unpredictably; use `shasum -a 256` for scope verification.\n   470\t- Run each `node tools/…/check-*.mjs` gate **standalone, one at a time** — chaining multiple node commands in one shell call produces spurious, non-reproducible errors in this environment.\n   471\t- Batch subdirectories: use existing `tools/p3-batch/`, `tools/p4-batch/`, etc. alongside the Math source files — do not overwrite Math source files.\n   472\t\n   473\t---\n   474\t\n   475\t## 16. Orthography house standard\n   476\t\n   477\tRulings by the user (fluent Hausa speaker) and TIMSAN; carried from all prior arcs. The linter ERROR list is canonical; add a word only on the user's explicit ruling.\n   478\t\n   479\t- `ƙwai` — \"egg.\"\n   480\t- `ɓera` — \"rat/mouse.\"\n   481\t- `kaɗan` — \"little/a bit.\"\n   482\t- `riƙa` — habitual marker.\n   483\t- `ɓoye` — \"to hide.\"\n   484\t- `kara` (unhooked) = plant \"stem/stalk\" only; `ƙara` = \"to add/increase\" — context-dependent WARNING.\n   485\t- `guga` (not `goga`) — friction.\n   486\t\n   487\tP3–P6 Social and Citizenship Studies terminology has begun. The M1 pilot locked the first term set in §9. Continue adding only user-ruled terms here as later slices surface them.\n   488\t\n   489\t---\n   490\t\n   491\t*Brief version: 2026-07-16 M2 build-complete source-only. Status: awaiting M2 review before M3.*\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
